@startuml
title Token lifecycle — pause, the one-way upgrade lock, and the terminal state

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam stateBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

[*] --> Live : genesis\nborn unpaused, unlocked, active

state Live {
  state "Transfers open" as open
  state "Transfers paused" as paused
  open --> paused : PauseTransfers(True)\ncan_pause power user
  paused --> open : PauseTransfers(False)\ncan_pause power user
}

state "Upgrades open" as uopen
state "Upgrades locked" as ulocked

[*] --> uopen : genesis
uopen --> ulocked : LockUpgrades\nadmin, refuses to re-lock
ulocked --> ulocked : RotateMintingScript refused\nUpgradeRegistryNode refused

Live --> Deactivated : DeactivateContract\nadmin signs, requires paused first

state Deactivated #FDEEEE {
  state "GlobalState unspendable\nevery branch rejected\nbefore dispatch" as tomb
}

Deactivated --> [*] : no exit\nno branch clears the flag

note right of uopen
  While open: the minting authority
  may be swapped, and the transfer and
  seizure logic re-pointed through the
  registry node. Both are admin-gated.
end note

note bottom of Deactivated
  Mint dies (MintSecurity can never run),
  the pause can never be lifted, and the
  transfer, seizure, denylist and
  power-user validators all refuse.
  Supply need not be zero: cancelled
  and immobilised are both supported.
end note
@enduml
